### Modification to Section 2: Decouple Controlled Vocabularies from Disk JSON

#### Operational Purpose
Eliminates the architectural circularity and disk I/O dependency in `gdacore.vocabulary_manager`, which previously read `schemas/defs/_enums.schema.json` directly from disk. Re-anchors `GDAVocabularyManager` and the `schemas/defs/` directory definition to the procedural compilation model, establishing in-memory Python definitions in `gdaschema._schema_defs` as the authoritative single source of truth.

#### Updated Description: `schemas/defs/`
Under **Schema Definitions & Architecture (`schemas/`)**, replace the existing `schemas/defs/` entry with:
* `schemas/defs/`: Base data types, field definitions, reusable primitives, and compiled enum constraints. Generated directly via `gdaschema` procedural builders and audited via `gsm.py`.

#### Updated Description: `src/gdacore/vocabulary_manager.py`
Under **Permanent Automation & Tooling Suite (`tools/lib/gdacore/`)**, replace the existing `src/gdacore/vocabulary_manager.py` entry with:
* `src/gdacore/vocabulary_manager.py`: Centralized controlled vocabulary registry (`GDAVocabularyManager`, aliased as `GDASchemaEnums` / `SchemaEnums`) resolving domain terms directly from procedural schema definitions into immutable, attribute-accessible `VocabularySet` containers without disk I/O.